# Ignore everything in this directory
*

# Except .gitignore and dotenv file
!.gitignore
!.prometheus.yml
!.env.example
!.env.secrets.example

# Provisioning-as-code: dashboards, alerting rules, and the datasource
# definition are authored config with no secrets in them (alert contact
# points use ${GRAFANA_ALERT_EMAIL_TO}-style env var placeholders, not real
# values), meant to ship with the repo like any other committed config.
# Previously swept up by the blanket `*` above along with genuine runtime
# state, which silently left this whole tree untracked; test_observability.py
# already asserts on specific dashboard content and has never had a
# committed copy to check on a fresh clone.
#
# grafana.ini is the odd one out: it carries a real admin_password
# (rotate-passwords.sh's own rotation target), so only its .example ships,
# seeded the same way as every other app's live config.
!config/
!config/grafana.ini.example
!config/provisioning/
!config/provisioning/**

# Secret files consumed via compose `secrets:`. Real values stay ignored
# by the blanket `*` above; only the .example templates are committed.
!secrets/
secrets/*
!secrets/*.example
